{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"910","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. The Way to Home"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A frog lives on the axis "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Ox"},{"kind":"text","text":" and needs to reach home which is in the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". She starts from the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". The frog can jump to the right at a distance not more than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"d"},{"kind":"text","text":". So, after she jumped from the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" she can reach the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x + a"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" is an integer from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"d"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each point from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" is known if there is a lily flower in it. The frog can jump only in points with a lilies. Guaranteed that there are lilies in the points "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Determine the minimal number of jumps that the frog needs to reach home which is in the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". Consider that initially the frog is in the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". If the frog can not reach home, print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"d"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 100"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ d ≤ n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the point, which the frog wants to reach, and the maximal length of the frog jump."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains a string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" of length "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", consisting of zeros and ones. If a character of the string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" equals to zero, then in the corresponding point there is no lily flower. In the other case, in the corresponding point there is a lily flower. Guaranteed that the first and the last characters of the string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s"},{"kind":"text","text":" equal to one."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If the frog can not reach the home, print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the other case, print the minimal number of jumps that the frog needs to reach the home which is in the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8 4\n10010101\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 2\n1001\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8 4\n11100101\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"12 3\n101111100101\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example the from can reach home in two jumps: the first jump from the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" (the length of the jump is three), and the second jump from the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"8"},{"kind":"text","text":" (the length of the jump is four)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example the frog can not reach home, because to make it she need to jump on a distance three, but the maximum length of her jump equals to two."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"910A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/910/problem/A"}